<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<RecordType xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        RecordType.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API. Do not paste this back into
        <description>. NOTE ALSO: the comment must sit INSIDE the root element - a comment
        placed ABOVE <RecordType> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        THE DIRECT, UNLISTED DISPOSITION PATH. NINE STAGES:
        Disposition Readiness, Broker Selection, NDA, Release Materials, Offer Selection,
        LOI, PSA, Closing, Sale Closes.

        No broker is MARKETED THROUGH, so BOV Outreach and Active Listing are restricted out.
        A broker is still NAMED - Broker Selection is on this path too, and on this path the
        Broker Selection to NDA hop is owned by the adapted Broker_Selection_Approval rather
        than by a manual Advance button.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 RETRACTED 2026-08-19 - THE "NO BROKER, THEREFORE NO BROKER STAGE" NARRATIVE IS DEAD,
        AND SO IS ITS ON-MARKET MIRROR.
        =====================================================================================
        The superseded paragraph is quoted and retracted rather than deleted, because its shape
        (a stage list justified by "no broker is engaged") is what a future reader would rebuild
        from if it were simply removed:

            RETRACTED: "No broker is engaged, so there is no BOV Outreach, no Active Listing and
            no Call for Offers - those three stages are restricted OUT here. Disposition_Stage__c
            is restricted to the SEVEN off-market stages."

        WHAT REPLACED IT: an off-market deal DOES engage a broker - it just does not run a BOV
        beauty parade or a public listing. The client's redefinition adds Broker Selection,
        Release Materials, Offer Selection and Sale Closes here, and Disposition Offer is
        retired in favour of Offer Selection. What survives from that paragraph is only the
        narrow truth: BOV Outreach and Active Listing are still restricted out, because those
        two are genuinely marketing-side.

        🔴 THE SISTER DOCTRINE IS ALSO DEAD: "NDA and Disposition Offer are off-market stage
        values ONLY", which stood in On_Market.recordType-meta.xml, in
        All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression and in lwc/dispositionSidebar.js. NDA IS NOW ON BOTH
        PATHS. Nine of this type's eleven listed values are shared with On_Market, so THE STAGE
        VALUE NO LONGER IDENTIFIES THE PATH - test Disposition__c.Is_On_Market__c (or the record
        type itself) instead.

        =====================================================================================
        THE TRANSITION-WINDOW UNION - WHY THIS LIST HAS 11 VALUES AND NOT 9.
        =====================================================================================
        Disposition Offer and Completed are RETIRED but still listed. A metadata deploy CANNOT
        delete a picklist value, so they still exist on Disposition_Stage__c until a manual
        Setup deletion wave removes them; and a record type cannot reference a value that no
        longer exists, so they must be listed here until that wave runs and Salesforce drops
        them from this type automatically. This list is therefore old-values UNION new-values.
        ⚠ THEY WILL RENDER AS TWO UNGUIDED PATH STEPS after Sale Closes until the wave runs,
        because Disposition_Path_Off_Market has no step for either. That is cosmetic and it
        affects zero records - an org sweep on 2026-08-19 found no Disposition__c row on any
        retired value, and no Off_Market row at all.

        Sell_Decision_Trigger__c is enumerated in full because a record type file must list
        EVERY picklist on the object or values are silently dropped from that type.
        Disposition__c has exactly two picklists today.

        No <businessProcess> - that element is for Opportunity, Case, Lead and Solution only.

        ⚠ RECORD-TYPE PICKLIST RESTRICTION IS UI-ONLY. An API, seed or data-load write can put
        an on-market value on an off-market row. The gates that MATTER are the validation rules
        and the server-side asserts in DispositionApprovalService, not this list.
    -->
    <fullName>Off_Market</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>The direct, unlisted path, 9 stages: Readiness, Broker Selection, NDA, Release Materials, Offer Selection, LOI, PSA, Closing, Sale Closes. BOV Outreach and Active Listing are restricted out. Disposition Offer and Completed are retired, pending deletion.</description>
    <label>Off Market</label>
    <picklistValues>
        <picklist>Disposition_Stage__c</picklist>
        <values>
            <fullName>Disposition Readiness</fullName>
            <default>true</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Broker Selection</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>NDA</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Release Materials</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Offer Selection</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>LOI</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>PSA</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Closing</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Sale Closes</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <!-- RETIRED, transition window only. See the note above. -->
        <values>
            <fullName>Disposition Offer</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
        </values>
        <values>
            <fullName>Completed</fullName>
            <default>false</default>
